#: R/texts.R
msgid ""
"SARIMA extends ARIMA by adding a seasonal component (P, D, Q, s) that "
"explicitly models the repetition of patterns every s periods (for example, "
"every 12 months in monthly data). Use it when the series shows a clear, "
"recognizable seasonal pattern — sales with holiday peaks, electricity "
"consumption with daily or weekly cycles, tourism with a high season — that "
"a plain ARIMA could not capture. It is this module's default model "
"precisely because it covers the most frequent case in applied practice. In "
"exchange for that added power, it requires more historical data (ideally "
"several complete cycles) and a correctly specified periodicity (frequency)."
msgstr ""

